11
01:03:24,705 --> 01:03:30,705
Shag (also known as Shag: The Movie) is a 1988 teen romantic comedy film directed by Zelda Barron and starring Phoebe
Cates, Scott Coffey, Bridget Fonda, Annabeth Gish, Page Hannah, Robert Rusler, and Tyrone Power Jr.

12
01:09:10,588 --> 01:09:16,588
Set in 1963, the film follows four teenage girls who spend their last weekend together
in Myrtle Beach, South Carolina, before one of the girls gets married.

13
01:14:56,470 --> 01:15:02,470
The film features Carolina shag dancing and was produced in
cooperation with the South Carolina Film Commission.

14
01:20:42,352 --> 01:20:48,352
An international co-production between the United States and the United Kingdom, Shag was released in the UK on
August 12, 1988, by Palace Pictures and in the US on July 21, 1989, by Hemdale Film Corporation.

15
01:26:28,235 --> 01:26:34,235
The film explores themes of dance, beach, summer, boyfriend, woman director.

16
01:32:14,117 --> 01:32:20,117
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
